00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:01.010
So this is what
the TypeScript is doing or

00:05:01.011 --> 00:05:03.420
Google's GW key
compiler is doing.

00:05:03.421 --> 00:05:06.190
And there's another option is
that you provide better two

00:05:06.191 --> 00:05:07.830
chain support for
JavaScript language.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.890
So right now there are a couple
of tools that are widely adopted

00:05:12.891 --> 00:05:15.540
in the industry for
JavaScript development.

00:05:15.541 --> 00:05:18.251
