00:51:28.675 --> 00:51:31.574
be manifested as
a runtime pattern between

00:51:31.575 --> 00:51:36.100
the Node.js application and
the underlying operating system.

00:51:36.101 --> 00:51:40.200
It can be formalized as just
a single pattern of the system

00:51:40.201 --> 00:51:42.820
call from the Node general
application to the online

00:51:42.821 --> 00:51:45.740
operating systems and it can be
detected by this kind of tool.

00:51:48.430 --> 00:51:52.640
There are many other interesting
malicious packages of

00:51:52.641 --> 00:51:55.540
security vulnerabilities
that we found in the NPM.

00:51:55.541 --> 00:51:57.315
We also found a worm in NPM, so

00:51:57.316 --> 00:52:00.368
what it happens is that if
you install the package,

00:52:00.369 --> 00:52:04.810
it will self-replicate and
publish itself on the NPM again.

00:52:04.811 --> 00:52:11.840
And we also have some pranked
NPM packages like Rockstar.

00:52:11.841 --> 00:52:14.880
What happens is that if you
